\includegraphics[width=\columnwidth]{figures/fig_degeneracy_lp_scatter.pdf}
\caption{Instance degeneracy vs.\ LP selection gain. Blue circles: cross-dataset ($n{=}3$). Orange triangles: per-entity-type within Few-NERD ($n{=}8$, $\rho{=}{-}0.881$, $p{=}0.004$). The dashed line at ${\sim}$15\%\protect\footnotemark{} separates regimes where LP improves (left) vs.\ fails (right).}
\label{fig:degeneracy_scatter}
\end{figure}

\footnotetext{Boundary between Person (13.4\%, $+1.25$~pp) and Art (19.8\%, $-0.17$~pp).}

\paragraph{LP selection scales with sample budget.}
Doubling $N$ from 8 to 16 on Few-NERD yields $+0.52$~pp (paired $p{=}0.003$, CI $[+0.17, +0.87]$), driven by reduced degeneracy (14.6\% $\to$ 7.0\%) expanding headroom (12.1 $\to$ 15.4~pp), while LP ranking quality remains stable ($\rho{\approx}0.62$).
Structural signals remain uniformly negative at $N{=}16$; the gap persists regardless of sample budget.

\paragraph{Scale robustness.}
With Qwen3-4B (Table~\ref{tab:scale_ablation}), QE is comparable (mean $|\Delta\rho|{=}0.042$), yet selection remains below greedy despite 13.0~pp headroom. Task difficulty is a stronger predictor than model scale within the 3B--8B range (Appendix~\ref{app:llama3b}).
Degeneracy scales with capability: 8B shows 17.8\% vs.\ 4B's 10.4\% on SciERC (Table~\ref{tab:degeneracy}).

\paragraph{LoRA-rank ablation.}
Training with LoRA rank${=}8$ (vs.\ 32) lowers degeneracy from 17.8\% to 7.2\% and increases headroom to 16.0~pp, but selection still fails (LP 0.635 vs.\ greedy 0.640).
The ablation isolates the second condition: within-instance $\rho(\text{LP}, \text{F1}){\approx}0.24$ remains too weak despite wider LP spread (0.057 vs.\ 0.041 nats). Both low degeneracy and adequate alignment are independently necessary.

\paragraph{Supervised verifier baseline.}
Supervised verifiers (logistic regression, MLP, random forest) trained on all five signals (3-fold CV, SciERC, $N{=}16$, $+17.9$~pp headroom) all perform at or below greedy\footnote{Greedy F1 is 0.644 (3-seed mean), consistent with Table~\ref{tab:selection}.} (LR: $-0.3$~pp; MLP: $-0.6$~pp; RF: $-2.9$~pp).
Adding pairwise interaction features does not help (AUROC 0.632 vs.\ 0.639).
The bottleneck is in what the signals encode, not how they are aggregated.

